  "question": {
    "text": "For LED's to emit light in visible region of electromagnetic light, it should have energy band gap in the range of:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5yJCd",
      "text": "\n$0.1 \\mathrm{eV}$ to $0.4 \\mathrm{eV}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jCVbv",
      "text": "\n$0.5 \\mathrm{eV}$ to $0.8 \\mathrm{eV}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s1hWw",
      "text": "\n$0.9 \\mathrm{eV}$ to $1.6 \\mathrm{eV}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gYDy0",
      "text": "\n$1.7 \\mathrm{eV}$ to $3.0 \\mathrm{eV}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy band gap range is given by,\n$$\n\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{g}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda}\n$$\n\nFor visible region\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\lambda=\\left(4 \\times 10^{-7} \\sim 7 \\times 10^{-7}\\right) \\mathrm{m} \\\\\n&\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{g}}=\\frac{6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\times 3 \\times 10^8}{7 \\times 10^{-7}} \\\\\n&=\\frac{19.8 \\times 10^{-26}}{7 \\times 10^{-7}} \\\\\n&=\\frac{2.8 \\times 10^{-19}}{1.6 \\times 10^{-19}} \\\\\n&\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{g}}=1.75 \\mathrm{eV}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
